        <IRI>#Energy_unit</IRI>
        <Literal>Energy Unit</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="rdfs:comment"/>
        <IRI>#Fixed_Consumption</IRI>
        <Literal>Fixed Consumption Component represents uncontrollable consumption of energy from the connected domain.</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="rdfs:label"/>
        <IRI>#Fixed_Consumption</IRI>
        <Literal>Fixed Consumption</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="rdfs:comment"/>
        <IRI>#Fixed_Generation</IRI>
        <Literal>Fixed Generation Component represents uncontrollable generation of energy in the connected domain.</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="rdfs:label"/>
        <IRI>#Fixed_Generation</IRI>
        <Literal>Fixed Generation</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="rdfs:comment"/>
        <IRI>#Flexible_Consumption</IRI>
        <Literal>A Flexible Consumption Component allows the optimizer to define the energy consumption in the connected domain at each time step. The consumption can take the values from 0 to the value provided by max load parameter.</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="rdfs:label"/>
        <IRI>#Flexible_Consumption</IRI>
        <Literal>Flexible Consumption</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="rdfs:comment"/>
        <IRI>#Flexible_Generation</IRI>
        <Literal>Flexible generation component allows the optimizer to defines the energy generation in the connected domain at each time step. Generation can take the values from 0 to the value provided by max generation parameter. Cost of one unit of energy generation is provided by cost parameter.</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="rdfs:label"/>
        <IRI>#Flexible_Generation</IRI>
        <Literal>Flexible Generation</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="rdfs:label"/>
        <IRI>#Flow_unit</IRI>
        <Literal>Flow</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="rdfs:label"/>
        <IRI>#Gas</IRI>
        <Literal>Gas Domain</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="rdfs:label"/>
        <IRI>#Heat</IRI>
        <Literal>Heat Domain</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="rdfs:comment"/>
        <IRI>#Heat_Pump</IRI>
        <Literal>A Heat Pump Component is a special case of an Interconnector Component that connects a heat and electricity domain. It uses the same parameters as an Interconnector Component.</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="rdfs:label"/>
        <IRI>#Heat_Pump</IRI>
        <Literal>Heat Pump</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="rdfs:comment"/>
        <IRI>#Interconnector</IRI>
        <Literal>An Interconnector Component is connected to two domains. It consumes energy from one domain (specified by parameter domain from) and generates energy for another domain (specified by parameter domain to). The transformation is done with efficiency provided by parameter mu. It is the ratio of the energy generated in domain to to energy consumed in domain from. The consumption from the domain from can take the values from 0 to the value provided by max in parameter. The generation to the domain to can take the values from 0 to the value provided by max out parameter.</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="rdfs:label"/>
        <IRI>#Interconnector</IRI>
        <Literal>Interconnector</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="rdfs:label"/>
        <IRI>#Kilowatt</IRI>
        <Literal>Kilowatt</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="rdfs:label"/>
        <IRI>#Kilowatt_hours</IRI>
        <Literal>Kilowatt Hours</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="rdfs:label"/>
        <IRI>#Notification</IRI>
        <Literal>Notification</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="rdfs:comment"/>
        <IRI>#Optimizer_Component</IRI>
        <Literal>Optimization Components represent one or more Assets, aggregate their parameters and measurements and are consumed by an optimizer.</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="rdfs:label"/>
        <IRI>#Optimizer_Component</IRI>
        <Literal>Optimizer Component</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="rdfs:comment"/>
        <IRI>#Optimizer_Domain</IRI>
        <Literal>Each Optimizer Component either belongs to one Optimizer Domain or connects multiple.</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="rdfs:label"/>
        <IRI>#Optimizer_Domain</IRI>
        <Literal>Optimizer Domain</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
