    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="rdfs:comment"/>
        <IRI>#Storage</IRI>
        <Literal>A Storage Component allows the optimizer to define the energy generation and consumption in the connected domain at each time step. The storage component is capable of storing energy over multiple time steps. The maximum energy that can be stored in the component is defined by parameter max capacity. A capacity before first time step is provided by component initial capacity. The consumption (charge process) from the connected domain can take the values from 0 to the value provided by max charge parameter. The generation (discharge process) to the connected domain can take the values from 0 to the value provided by max discharge parameter. The efficiency of energy conversion is determined by parameter mu - the ratio between energy added to the storage of the component as a result of charging to the energy consumed from domain (or the ratio between energy that consumed from the storage to the energy generated in domain).</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="rdfs:label"/>
        <IRI>#Storage</IRI>
        <Literal>Storage</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="rdfs:comment"/>
        <IRI>#Tag</IRI>
        <Literal>Tags are key-value pairs with the key being &quot;Direction&quot;, &quot;Domain&quot; or &quot;Prediction Window&quot;. Each key may only have a value from a set of values that are specific to the key. For example, &quot;Domain&quot; only allows for the values of &quot;Electricity&quot; and &quot;Heat&quot;. A key-value pair such as &quot;Domain&quot; - &quot;Electricity&quot; is modelled as an instance of &quot;Domain&quot; with the value, which is of type string, being set to &quot;Electricity&quot;.</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="rdfs:label"/>
        <IRI>#Tag</IRI>
        <Literal>Tag</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="rdfs:label"/>
        <IRI>#Temperature_unit</IRI>
        <Literal>Temperature Unit</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="rdfs:comment"/>
        <IRI>#Time-shiftable_Load_Component</IRI>
        <Literal>A Time-shiftable Load Component allows the optimizer to define the energy consumption in the connected domain at time steps (inclusive) between parameters time from and time to. Note that time from and time to are the time steps in the interval, not timestamps. For example, if the optimization is performed for 15 minute intervals over the course of a day, there are 96 time steps, which the parameters refer to. During these time steps total consumption is equal to the parameter load. The consumption can take the values from 0 to the value provided by max parameter.</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="rdfs:label"/>
        <IRI>#Time-shiftable_Load_Component</IRI>
        <Literal>Time-shiftable Load Component</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="rdfs:comment"/>
        <IRI>#UI_Component</IRI>
        <Literal>UI components in information regarding the API is not extensively modeled in this ontology. Thus, they are summed up as UI_Component.</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="rdfs:label"/>
        <IRI>#UI_Component</IRI>
        <Literal>UI Component</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="rdfs:comment"/>
        <IRI>#Unit_of_measure</IRI>
        <Literal>Units of measure are used for measurements. Different units that are found in the data stored in the database are modeled here.</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="rdfs:label"/>
        <IRI>#Unit_of_measure</IRI>
        <Literal>Unit of Measure</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
